From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:26:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 114/121] DT1: draft-phase tail glue (SGLANG_OPT_DRAFT_TAIL,
 default off)

Bit-exact, one flag:
- EagerRunner: skip the registry input copy when it would be captured into
  the draft decode graph (the graph already feeds its own static buffers);
  saves 5-7 replayed copies per draft forward.
- Draft decode graph: fp32 next_token_logits_buffer, so the draft lm_head
  writes fp32 directly and the per-forward bf16->fp32 cast is gone.
- _draft_extend_for_decode, topk=1: one Triton select pass (rows from
  accept_lens in-kernel, split argmax, hidden row copy) replaces select_index,
  two gathers, argmax and ones_like.

SGLANG_OPT_DRAFT_TAIL_FUSED_CONF (default off, not bit-exact, ~2e-6 rel):
the adaptive position-0 confidence comes from the same select pass instead
of torch top1_prob.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
